Let's look at the number of toys a single elf makes. A single elf makes $x$ toys every hour and works $t$ hours. So in total, the elf makes $x\cdot t$ toys:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(x\,\dfrac{\text{toys}}{\text{hour}}\right)\left(t\,\text{hours}\right)
\\\\
&=x\cdot t\,\dfrac{\text{toys}}{\cancel{\text{hour}}}\cdot\,\cancel{\text{hours}}
\\\\
&=x\cdot t\,\text{toys}
\end{align}$
